WEBVTT

1
00:00:25.791 --> 00:00:30.041


2
00:00:30.041 --> 00:00:35.666
<b>Lord Krishna has just completed his profound </b>
<b>explanation of Nishkam Karma Yoga to Arjuna</b>

3
00:00:35.666 --> 00:00:42.500
<b>He has explained that in this practice, </b>
<b>Arjuna must focus solely on his actions,</b>

4
00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:47.041
<b>maintain equanimity in </b>
<b>both success and failure,</b>

5
00:00:47.041 --> 00:00:53.458
<b>and ensure that his actions are free from desire.</b>

6
00:00:53.458 --> 00:00:58.750
<b>Now, Krishna reveals what one achieves</b>
<b>through this path of selfless action.</b>

7
00:00:58.750 --> 00:01:02.041
<b>He explains that through Nishkam Karma Yoga,</b>

8
00:01:02.041 --> 00:01:06.583
<b>one can find liberation from both the positive </b>
<b>and negative consequences of their actions.</b>

9
00:01:06.583 --> 00:01:10.458
<b>Therefore, he urges Arjuna to master this skill,</b>

10
00:01:10.458 --> 00:01:16.875
<b>as this practice will bring excellence </b>
<b>and perfection to his actions.</b>

11
00:01:21.750 --> 00:01:24.125
<b>While the very foundation </b>
<b>of Nishkam Karma Yoga</b>

12
00:01:24.125 --> 00:01:29.291
<b>is to perform actions without </b>
<b>attachment to results,</b>

13
00:01:29.291 --> 00:01:33.166
<b>it's natural for Arjuna to have questions.</b>

14
00:01:33.166 --> 00:01:34.708
<b>He might wonder</b>

15
00:01:34.708 --> 00:01:39.208
<b>yes, one shouldn't desire results </b>
<b>in Nishkam Karma Yoga,</b>

16
00:01:39.208 --> 00:01:42.583
<b>but what is the ultimate </b>
<b>outcome of this entire practice?</b>

17
00:01:42.583 --> 00:01:46.125
<b>This question doesn't stem </b>
<b>from attachment to results,</b>

18
00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:49.083
<b>but rather from genuine curiosity.</b>

19
00:01:49.083 --> 00:01:51.500
<b>Just as every process has an outcome,</b>

20
00:01:51.500 --> 00:01:55.583
<b>what is the culmination of </b>
<b>this path of selfless action?</b>

21
00:01:55.583 --> 00:01:59.708
<b>Anticipating such questions, Krishna explains</b>

22
00:01:59.708 --> 00:02:02.416
<b>that one who practices Nishkam Karma Yoga</b>

23
00:02:02.416 --> 00:02:06.916
<b>becomes free from all</b>
<b>consequences of their actions.</b>

24
00:02:06.916 --> 00:02:09.625
<b>This is particularly significant for Arjuna,</b>

25
00:02:09.625 --> 00:02:12.833
<b>who was distressed about</b>

26
00:02:12.833 --> 00:02:21.000
<b>incurring sin and facing negative consequences </b>
<b>for causing the death of his loved ones in battle.</b>

27
00:02:21.000 --> 00:02:23.833
<b>Krishna's answer addresses this very concern</b>

28
00:02:23.833 --> 00:02:29.416
<b>through the practice of selfless action, </b>
<b>you will be liberated from all consequences.</b>

29
00:02:29.416 --> 00:02:32.666
<b>You will break free from the bondage of karma.</b>

30
00:02:32.666 --> 00:02:37.083
<b>As the saying goes, "Diamond cuts diamond"</b>

31
00:02:37.083 --> 00:02:39.250
<b>similarly, understand</b>

32
00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:44.083
<b>that the path to freedom from karmic </b>
<b>bonds lies through action itself.</b>

33
00:02:44.083 --> 00:02:45.791
<b>Nishkam Karma Yoga</b>

34
00:02:45.791 --> 00:02:48.583
<b>liberates one from the chains of karma.</b>

35
00:02:48.583 --> 00:02:52.000
<b>However, there's a potential pitfall here.</b>

36
00:02:52.000 --> 00:02:55.583
<b>If one practices selfless action with </b>
<b>a desperate desire for liberation,</b>

37
00:02:55.583 --> 00:02:59.833
<b>that very desire will render</b>
<b>the practice ineffective.</b>

38
00:02:59.833 --> 00:03:05.291
<b>Walking this path is like balancing on a tightrope.</b>

39
00:03:05.291 --> 00:03:06.458
<b>That's why</b>

40
00:03:06.458 --> 00:03:12.750
<b>Krishna uses the phrase </b>
<b>'Karmasu Kaushalam' in this verse</b>

41
00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:15.708
<b>the skill in action,</b>

42
00:03:15.708 --> 00:03:17.666
<b>the art of performing action.</b>

43
00:03:17.666 --> 00:03:25.083
<b>No art or skill becomes easy until it's </b>
<b>practiced consistently.</b>

44
00:03:25.083 --> 00:03:32.333
<b>This is why Krishna urges Arjuna to </b>
<b>practice this challenging skill.</b>

45
00:03:37.250 --> 00:03:44.625
<b>When one accomplishes good deeds,</b>
<b>praise and fame follow naturally.</b>

46
00:03:44.625 --> 00:03:48.000
<b>This experience brings great joy.</b>

47
00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:55.875
<b>However, when mistakes occur, </b>
<b>criticism and even contempt may follow.</b>

48
00:03:55.875 --> 00:03:59.208
<b>This becomes a painful experience.</b>

49
00:03:59.208 --> 00:04:04.750
<b>Even when work is done to </b>
<b>one's satisfaction and excellence,</b>

50
00:04:04.750 --> 00:04:08.625
<b>if most people criticize it,</b>

51
00:04:08.625 --> 00:04:12.958
<b>the experience remains distressing.</b>

52
00:04:12.958 --> 00:04:21.875
<b>In all these situations, the feelings of</b>
<b>joy, sorrow, and pain revolve around one thing</b>

53
00:04:21.875 --> 00:04:25.208
<b>people's reactions.</b>

54
00:04:25.208 --> 00:04:30.708
<b>Whether they approved of your work or not.</b>

55
00:04:30.708 --> 00:04:34.541
<b>Often, influenced by such experiences,</b>

56
00:04:34.541 --> 00:04:40.416
<b>one begins to act merely to please others.</b>

57
00:04:40.416 --> 00:04:41.791
<b>Take for instance...</b>

58
00:04:41.791 --> 00:04:49.708
<b>a musician who abandons their </b>
<b>inherited superior style for a new one.</b>

59
00:04:49.708 --> 00:04:53.375
<b>This new style brings no inner satisfaction,</b>

60
00:04:53.375 --> 00:04:54.208
<b>yet</b>

61
00:04:54.208 --> 00:05:03.458
<b>being trendy, it promises </b>
<b>maximum praise and recognition.</b>

62
00:05:03.458 --> 00:05:04.791
<b>In this process,</b>

63
00:05:04.791 --> 00:05:13.625
<b>they sacrifice their contentment and </b>
<b>compromise their artistic principles.</b>

64
00:05:13.625 --> 00:05:21.666
<b>The consequences will surface </b>
<b>when musical trends shift again.</b>

65
00:05:21.666 --> 00:05:23.416
<b>In such times,</b>

66
00:05:23.416 --> 00:05:29.208
<b>the musician will be left with </b>
<b>neither satisfaction nor fame.</b>

67
00:05:29.208 --> 00:05:30.416
<b>But</b>

68
00:05:30.416 --> 00:05:38.750
<b>if we perform our duties guided by inner </b>
<b>satisfaction rather than people's reactions,</b>

69
00:05:38.750 --> 00:05:43.166
<b>no one can take away our joy.</b>

70
00:05:43.166 --> 00:05:47.708
<b>This extends to the higher principle </b>
<b>of Nishkama Karma Yoga,</b>

71
00:05:47.708 --> 00:05:54.916
<b>where one must focus solely on </b>
<b>their actions, not the results.</b>

72
00:05:54.916 --> 00:05:59.833
<b>Thus, favorable outcomes don't breed ego,</b>

73
00:05:59.833 --> 00:06:04.916
<b>nor do unfavorable ones cause distress.</b>

74
00:06:04.916 --> 00:06:10.250
<b>Such balance in action is an art itself</b>

75
00:06:10.250 --> 00:06:12.208
<b>"Karmasu Kaushalam"</b>

76
00:06:12.208 --> 00:06:14.333
<b>the art of performing actions</b>

77
00:06:14.333 --> 00:06:19.750
<b>This is the art I'm inspiring Arjuna to practice.</b>

78
00:06:19.750 --> 00:06:24.333
<b>Would you like to learn this art?</b>

79
00:06:29.041 --> 00:06:33.125
<b>Humans are vessels of imperfection.</b>

80
00:06:33.125 --> 00:06:36.208
<b>Everyone makes mistakes.</b>

81
00:06:36.208 --> 00:06:37.041
<b>But</b>

82
00:06:37.041 --> 00:06:42.458
<b>when we learn the right lessons from </b>
<b>these mistakes according to our understanding,</b>

83
00:06:42.458 --> 00:06:46.958
<b>when we bring positive improvements</b>
<b>to our future efforts,</b>

84
00:06:46.958 --> 00:06:52.958
<b>we no longer face the consequences </b>
<b>of past errors.</b>

85
00:06:52.958 --> 00:06:54.708
<b>For example,</b>

86
00:06:54.708 --> 00:06:58.916
<b>if someone in your family fails an exam,</b>

87
00:06:58.916 --> 00:07:02.041
<b>but they understand their mistake,</b>

88
00:07:02.041 --> 00:07:04.375
<b>correct themselves,</b>

89
00:07:04.375 --> 00:07:09.916
<b>and pass with good marks next time </b>
<b>through dedicated effort,</b>

90
00:07:09.916 --> 00:07:13.750
<b>the impact of the previous failure fades away.</b>

91
00:07:13.750 --> 00:07:16.958
<b>You should learn this lesson yourself</b>

92
00:07:16.958 --> 00:07:20.458
<b>and teach it to the younger ones in your family.</b>

93
00:07:20.458 --> 00:07:22.708
<b>If a mistake happens,</b>

94
00:07:22.708 --> 00:07:24.458
<b>it's alright.</b>

95
00:07:24.458 --> 00:07:29.000
<b>Instead of being distressed by that error,</b>

96
00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:33.291
<b>simply learn from it, improve, and try again.</b>

97
00:07:33.291 --> 00:07:34.625
<b>New results</b>

98
00:07:34.625 --> 00:07:38.500
<b>will erase the effects of old mistakes.</b>

99
00:07:38.500 --> 00:07:42.208
<b>This is precisely how </b>
<b>Nishkama Karma Yoga works</b>

100
00:07:42.208 --> 00:07:47.416
<b>where by improving our actions, </b>
<b>making them selfless,</b>

101
00:07:47.416 --> 00:07:52.791
<b>the consequences of all past </b>
<b>actions and mistakes are erased.</b>

102
00:07:52.791 --> 00:07:56.041
<b>Liberation follows.</b>

103
00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:08.958
<b>People learn and apply various </b>
<b>arts in their workplace.</b>

104
00:08:08.958 --> 00:08:10.625
<b>The art of communication,</b>

105
00:08:10.625 --> 00:08:12.416
<b>the art of training,</b>

106
00:08:12.416 --> 00:08:15.041
<b>the art of leadership...</b>

107
00:08:15.041 --> 00:08:16.250
<b>Perhaps</b>

108
00:08:16.250 --> 00:08:18.458
<b>you'll say</b>

109
00:08:18.458 --> 00:08:19.708
<b>that communication,</b>

110
00:08:19.708 --> 00:08:20.875
<b>training,</b>

111
00:08:20.875 --> 00:08:22.083
<b>and leadership</b>

112
00:08:22.083 --> 00:08:24.666
<b>are routine tasks?</b>

113
00:08:24.666 --> 00:08:29.416
<b>Why call them arts?</b>

114
00:08:29.416 --> 00:08:31.541
<b>Understand this distinction...</b>

115
00:08:31.541 --> 00:08:34.583
<b>Anyone can communicate,</b>

116
00:08:34.583 --> 00:08:35.875
<b>but</b>

117
00:08:35.875 --> 00:08:39.875
<b>effective communication is an art.</b>

118
00:08:39.875 --> 00:08:42.833
<b>Anyone can train,</b>

119
00:08:42.833 --> 00:08:55.250
<b>but delivering training that is both </b>
<b>enjoyable and memorable is an art.</b>

120
00:08:55.250 --> 00:08:58.541
<b>Work is merely the name of an activity;</b>

121
00:08:58.541 --> 00:09:02.791
<b>art is making that activity excellent.</b>

122
00:09:02.791 --> 00:09:04.416
<b>For instance,</b>

123
00:09:04.416 --> 00:09:08.375
<b>cooking tasty food is a chef's job,</b>

124
00:09:08.375 --> 00:09:09.291
<b>but</b>

125
00:09:09.291 --> 00:09:18.166
<b>a skilled chef not only makes the</b>
<b>food delicious but serves it creatively,</b>

126
00:09:18.166 --> 00:09:24.000
<b>performing this activity with such excellence</b>

127
00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:26.583
<b>that neither does the kitchen get messy,</b>

128
00:09:26.583 --> 00:09:31.250
<b>nor do their white clothes get stained.</b>

129
00:09:31.250 --> 00:09:38.333
<b>Here, that skilled chef has mastered </b>
<b>the art of making an activity excellent.</b>

130
00:09:38.333 --> 00:09:43.916
<b>Here, I am inspiring Arjuna</b>
<b>to practice the art of karma.</b>

131
00:09:43.916 --> 00:09:49.000
<b>That is, to practice making his actions excellent.</b>

132
00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:55.916
<b>And the supreme action is </b>
<b>one without attachment to results.</b>

133
00:09:55.916 --> 00:10:00.708
<b>That indeed is Nishkama Karma Yoga.</b>

134
00:10:00.708 --> 00:10:07.958
<b>Would you like to learn this art </b>
<b>of making actions excellent? </b>

135
00:10:07.958 --> 00:10:10.583
<b>This art has many aspects,</b>

136
00:10:10.583 --> 00:10:13.875
<b>which will be detailed ahead.</b>

137
00:10:13.875 --> 00:10:15.875
<b>Stay connected.</b>

